      "body": "# [deps] upgrade vllm to 0.28.0\r\n\r\n# What does this PR do?\r\n\r\nFixes # (issue)\r\n\r\nRaises the vLLM version ceiling from `<=0.11.0` to `<0.29.0` so the vLLM inference backend can be used on Intel XPU.\r\n\r\nvLLM only publishes prebuilt Intel XPU wheels from 0.28.0 onwards, so every XPU build is rejected by the current check:\r\n\r\n```\r\n  File \"src/llamafactory/hparams/parser.py\", line 272, in _check_extra_dependencies\r\n    check_version(\"vllm>=0.4.3,<=0.11.0\")\r\nImportError: vllm>=0.4.3,<=0.11.0 is required for a normal functioning of this module, but found vllm==0.28.0+xpu.\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Changes\r\n\r\n- `src/llamafactory/hparams/parser.py`: `vllm>=0.4.3,<=0.11.0` → `vllm>=0.4.3,<0.29.0`\r\n- `requirements/vllm.txt`: same\r\n\r\nNo code changes are needed; `vllm_engine.py` works unmodified with 0.28.0.\r\n\r\n### Testing\r\n\r\nIntel Arc Pro B60, Python 3.12.13, vllm 0.28.0+xpu, torch 2.13.0+xpu, transformers 5.8.0.\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nllamafactory-cli chat examples/inference/qwen3.yaml infer_backend=vllm\r\n```\r\n\r\n| | Result |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| Before | `ImportError` above |\r\n| After, 1 card | correct response |\r\n| After, 2 cards (tensor parallel) | correct response |\r\n\r\nNot tested on CUDA.\r\n\r\n## Before submitting\r\n\r\n- [x] Did you read the [contributor guideline](https://github.com/hiyouga/LLaMA-Factory/blob/main/.github/CONTRIBUTING.md)?\r\n- [ ] Did you write any new necessary tests?\r\n",
